onerutter.com is Jake Rutter's personal site (Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript, MDX, Vercel from `main`). The canonical agent guide is `AGENTS.md`. Prefer the code over `PLAN.md` when they disagree.

Commands that exist: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint` (`eslint`), `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`). Run lint, typecheck, and build before pushing. There is no test script.

Before using a Next.js API, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. The `nextjs-agent-rules` block in `AGENTS.md` is managed by `next dev`; leave it in place.

Content rules:

- Do not mention a planned move. A future return to the US stays off the site.
- Do not invent trip details, captions, place names, or biographical facts.
- Do not expose exact photo locations. GPS stays out of committed images. `places` coordinates are country or city centroids at two decimal places, never a street or a photo spot.
- Keep Jake's wording for the story copy in `app/story/page.tsx`. The timeline in `lib/story.ts` is marked “Needs an edit”; do not silently rewrite it. The story page lists those entries newest year first.
- `draft: true` stays out of production HTML, the RSS feed, and the sitemap. Publishing is `draft: false`.
- Do not add a project, note, or trip Jake has not asked for.
- Do not publish an email address or a `mailto:` link. `/hello` is how to reach Jake.

Canonical URL is `https://onerutter.com` in `lib/site.ts`. It is not an environment variable. Pull requests stay small. Run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build` before pushing. Skip screenshots. When the Vercel preview is ready, include the preview URL of each changed page in the pull request and in the report.
